<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18138" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄφαντ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαίνομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>made invisible, blotted out,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκήδεστοι καὶ ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.60
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσπερμος γενεὴ καὶ ἄ. ὄληται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					20.303
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <i>hidden,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ἕρμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1007
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔφην᾽ ἄφαντον φῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					297
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ἔπελες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					1.46
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ βροτῶν ἄ. βῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					832
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁνὴρ ἄ. ἐκ . . στρατοῦ</span>
			he has <i>disappeared,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				624
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. οἴχεσθαι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				657
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				2.59a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρρειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					560
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρθεῖσ᾽ ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					606
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ χερῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					827
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴχνος πλατᾶν ἄ.</span>
			<i>disappearing,</i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				695
			</span></i> (lyr.); <i>invisible,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parm.
					9.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>in secret,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄφαντα βρέμειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					11.30
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>obscure,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>N.</u>
				8.34
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοῖς δῆλος θνητοῖσι δ᾽
			ἄ.</span> Epimenid.II.—Poet. and late Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. γενέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					3.60
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				4.65
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				24.31
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἄφαντα φήναντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.
					1.260
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>, cf. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				899
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
